{
  "id": "06-listen-and-write",
  "title": "Listen, Write, and Act",
  "tenet": "Offer your goals to God",
  "durationMs": 74760,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/06-listen-and-write.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/06-listen-and-write.json",
  "text": "What if the next answer to your prayer begins with a step you would rather postpone?\n\nA woman came to prayer with a goal she cared deeply about. She wanted to begin work that would help her neighborhood. She opened a notebook and asked God for mercy and guidance. In the quiet she remembered a colleague she had dismissed too quickly. She wrote the thought down, then waited. Later she tested it against Scripture, love, and the counsel of someone she trusted. She did not call every thought a message from God. But she knew an honest apology would be good. The next day she made it. Their conversation became the first small step toward the work she hoped to do.\n\nCooperation with grace has room for listening and for action. Name a goal that matters. Set a daily or weekly period and bring a notebook. Begin by entrusting the time to God. Sit, listen, and write what arises without forcing an answer. Then discern patiently: does it agree with Christ's love and with wise counsel? Choose one faithful action within your reach. If the page stays blank, the time is still prayer. Return at the next appointed time. A willing heart is formed through attention, truth, and service.",
